## v1.0.0b3
+ Add `--workon <project>` option to the `celebi` CLI entry point. It switches the current project before starting the Chern shell, e.g. `celebi --workon my-analysis`. Unknown project names are reported and the shell is not started.
+ Improve path completion in the Chern shell.
  - `@` is no longer a word delimiter, so `@/` project-root paths complete as a single token.
  - Dotfiles and dot-directories are hidden by default and appear once the typed segment starts with a dot.
  - Bare `.` acts as a hidden-prefix search in the current directory instead of a directory shortcut; `..` still walks up.
  - `@/` completion results are restricted to the project root.
+ Fix stageout export for predecessor outputs with nested paths (e.g. `subdir/file.root`). The parent directory is now created per output file instead of assuming a flat `stageout/` directory, so nested outputs no longer fail to export.
+ Refactor `add_source` to store the source MD5 via `set_input_md5` instead of writing `data.json` directly, matching the rawdata workflow used by Yuki's `use-data` command.
+ Add regression tests for nested stageout directory creation and shell path completion.
+ Add a command naming review report (`COMMAND_NAMING_REVIEW.md`) covering the `celebi`, `celebi-cli`, `celebi-git`, and Chern shell command surfaces.
+ Rename the data commands to directional verbs.
  - `use-data` -> `attach-data`: adopt an impression already on DITE as a local raw-data task (no data transfer).
  - `send` -> `upload-data`: upload a local directory to DITE with a progress bar.
  - The old names are removed entirely.
+ Add `register-data <runner> <remote_path> [--descriptor]`: register data that already lives on an SSH runner.
  - The MD5 is computed on the runner; the data is copied into Yuki's managed impressions area on that runner — it never crosses the local network.
  - Registration runs as a background job on Yuki (hashing → copying → registering) with live progress; re-registering the same path is idempotent.
  - On success the current raw-data task is filled (or a pointer task created) and its default runner is set to the runner hosting the data.
+ Add `verify-data`: recompute the MD5 of the current data task and compare it with the registered UUID (remote data is re-hashed on its host runner).
+ Add `cache_on_runner` task option (shell: `cache_on_runner on|off`), replacing `use_eos`.
  - REANA runner: results are copied to EOS.
  - SSH runner: results are copied to the runner's managed impressions area.
  - native/dry: no effect.
  - The task option is transmitted to Yuki at submit time.
+ Runner management overhaul.
  - `register-runner` now accepts ssh options (`--ssh-host/--ssh-user/--ssh-key-path/--ssh-port/--remote-workdir`) and native options (`--workdir/--cores/--mem-mb/--conda-path/--snakemake-path`); `update-runner` accepts the same options.
  - SSH private keys are uploaded automatically at register/update (a client-side path is read and sent; the server stores the key). Registration falls back to `~/.ssh/id_rsa` / `~/.ssh/id_ed25519` when no key path is given.
  - Add `test-runner <name>`: probes connectivity, snakemake, conda and the remote working directory; results are persisted and shown by `runners` (HEALTH column).
  - Add `runner-envs <name>`: lists the conda environments available on an ssh/native runner.
  - The Chern shell gains `test_runner`, `runner_envs`, `register_data`, `cache_on_runner`, and runner-name tab completion; `register_runner` in the shell is now ssh-aware.
+ Raw-data task display and status.
  - `ls` no longer shows Memory limit / Validated for raw-data tasks; it shows Cache on runner instead of Use EOS.
  - `status` renders the stageout file table (name/size/type/in-Yuki marks) for raw-data tasks, falling back to the sample-files listing.
  - `archived` displays as `[coda][archived]`.
+ Engine logs.
  - `engine-logs` renders the ssh/native log schema (`workflow_log`/`snakemake_log`); the workflow log section is titled YUKI LOG.
  - `engine-logs --fetch` generates the engine logs on the server when they are missing; without `--fetch` the Yuki workflow log is still served when available.
  - Error bodies (e.g. log not found) are shown as errors instead of an empty N/A table.
+ Fix the DITE port fallback (`127.0.0.1:3315` instead of `localhost:5000`), the `add_host` wrapper arity mismatch, and the never-populated runner tab-completion cache.
+ Declare the `tqdm` dependency (used by the upload progress bar) in `pyproject.toml`.
+ Fix all pylint issues across `CelebiChrono` (10.00/10 with the project rcfile).
+ Bump version to 1.0.0b3.

## v1.0.0b2
+ Add project-root-relative path support in the Chern shell. Paths starting with `@/` (or bare `@`) in `add-input`, `add-algorithm`, and `add-parameter-subtask` are resolved relative to the current project root, making it easier to reference objects from anywhere in the project. Tab completion also understands `@/` prefixes.
+ Improve `collect` feedback and error reporting.
  - Print a `Collecting '<selector>' from impression <id>...` start message.
  - Surface HTTP/connection errors instead of silently returning the error body.
  - Warn when no files are currently collected.
  - Report the number of files now in Yuki after a successful collect.
  - Display skipped and failed files with reasons when the Yuki server returns a collect report.
+ Add selective impress/submit by object names. In the shell, `impress a b` operates only on the named sub-objects while the no-argument form continues to process all sub-objects collectively. `submit` accepts an optional `--runner <name>` flag and any remaining positional arguments as object names, e.g. `submit --runner cern a b` or `submit a b`.
+ Add `--reference <algorithm>` option to the shell `workaround` command. It copies the referenced algorithm into a `reference/` subdirectory of the workaround space for side-by-side code inspection. Add `--skip-input <task>` option to skip mounting the impression of a specified input task. Both options have tab-completion support in the shell.
+ Add filelist manifest for the workaround workflow. `workaround_preshell` records the initial algorithm files to `filelist.yaml`, and `workaround_postshell` copies files in the manifest to origin while deleting files in origin that are not listed.
+ Add LHCb Analysis Productions (AP) data list task type (`lhcb_ap_datalist`).
  - `create-lhcb-ap-list` command creates the task with example AP configuration.
  - `add-apd-token` command stores the APD token in `.celebi/config.local.json`.
  - `ls` shows `temp_apd_token` status for these tasks.
+ Deposit uploads `.celebi/config.local.json` alongside the impression so Yuki can generate `lbapi_key.json` server-side.
+ Mark `datalist` and `lhcb_ap_datalist` tasks as validated without requiring an algorithm.
+ Add runner management utilities.
  - `update-runner <name>` command to modify runner settings (URL, token, backend type, Kerberos, EOS mount point).
  - `runners` command now displays full runner configuration.
+ Fix arc cache invalidation so `add-algorithm`/`remove-input` changes are visible immediately in `ls`.
+ Add unit test for arc cache invalidation.
+ Bump version to 1.0.0b2.
+ Fix `book-reana` streaming error message so a connection lost mid-upload is reported as "Connection to Yuki server ... was lost" instead of "Could not connect to Yuki server".
+ Add unit tests for streaming connection-loss scenarios (initial failure vs. mid-stream drop).
+ Refactor `CelebiChrono/interface/shell_modules/reana_booking.py` to reduce complexity and improve maintainability.
+ Resolve all remaining non-informational pylint warnings across `CelebiChrono`, bringing the full-project pylint score to 10.00/10.
+ Fix `status` display to use `status_musical` and `status_legacy` fields from the Yuki server, showing `[coda][finished]` for completed workflows instead of `[coda][coda]`.

## v1.0.0b1
+ Initial beta release of CelebiChrono.
